    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "727\nA IMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFOR OUR 727 FANJET PASSENGERS\nEven though you may be an experi\nenced air traveler, there are certain\nfeatures of this, the most modern of\nair transports, with which you may\nnot be familiar.\nPACIFIC SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\nAUTOMATIC OXYGEN SYSTEM\nThe higher altitudes at which this aircraft operates require the\nprompt use of the automatic oxygen system in case of any\nsudden change in cabin pressure. Should a decompression occur\noxygen masks will drop down. Take nearest mask and promptly\nplace over nose and mouth. Adjust Headband. Breathe normally.\nNO SMOKING\nFORWARD\nFACING\nSEAT\nBREATHE\nNORMALLY\nSEAT BELT\nEven if the \"SEAT BELT\" sign\nis turned off in flight, it is\nrecommended that you keep\nyour seat belt loosely fastened,\nwhenever you are in your seat.\nFLOTATION EQUIPMENT\nBRACING POSITION\nREAR\nFACING\nSEAT\nIn\nthe\nevent of a water landing,\ncushion may be used as an aid to\nkeep afloat. Grasp the cushion at the\nrear, pull it forward and take it with\nyou.\nPlace arms\nthrough straps on\nbottom to retain cushion.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT\nPSA-17\n6-21-68\nSEE REVERSE SIDE",
      "727\nB IMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFOR OUR 727 FANJET PASSENGERS\nPSA\nPACIFIC SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nThere are seven exits provided for your use. The chart below will\nshow you the one closest to your seat. The exits over the wings\nare removable windows. The two exits forward are doors which\nare equipped with fast operating evacuation slides.\nWINDOW EXITS\nSTEP 1\nSTEP 2\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nFORWARDE\nCABIN\nDOOR\nSLIDE\nPULL\nDOWN\nTHIS\nFLAP\nGRASP\nHANDLE\nAND\nPULL\nDOWN\nCABIN DOORS\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nSLIDE\nPULL\nTOP\nINWARD\nAND\nLIFT\nWINDOW\nEXITS\nWINDOW\n•EXITS\nROTATE\nHANDLE\nPUSH\nDOOR\nOUT\nTOPEN\nCLOSED\nSLIDE\nMAIN REAR\nCABIN DOOR\nPLACARDS GIVING\nSTEPS FOR OPERATION\nOF EVACUATION\nSLIDE\nARE LOCATED ON EACH\nDOOR. SLIDE IS SHOWN\nREADY FOR USE.\n=\nSEE REVERSE SIDE\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT\n6-21-68\n2007.011.067"
    ],
